        <div class="game_title are1">
            <h3> JIGSAW PUZZLES</h3>
            Jigsaw puzzles are a type of puzzle game that involves assembling various pieces to create a complete
            picture or design. Here's a brief overview:

            <br> <b> Components: </b>Jigsaw puzzles consist of small, interlocking pieces, typically made of cardboard
            or wood. These
            pieces must be assembled to form a larger image.

            <br> <b> Images:</b> The pictures on jigsaw puzzle pieces can vary widely, from landscapes and famous
            artworks to
            animals, scenes from movies, and more. The complexity of the image often determines the difficulty of the
            puzzle.

            <br> <B>Sizes: </B> Jigsaw puzzles come in various sizes and piece counts, ranging from small puzzles with a
            few dozen
            pieces to large, intricate puzzles with thousands of pieces.

            <br> <b> Assembly:</b> Solving a jigsaw puzzle involves finding the correct location for each piece based on
            its shape,
            color, and the image it forms. The pieces are designed to fit together in a specific way, making it a
            challenging and satisfying activity.

            <br> <b> Benefits: </b>Jigsaw puzzles are known to have cognitive and therapeutic benefits. They promote
            problem-solving
            skills, pattern recognition, and patience. They are also a relaxing and enjoyable pastime for many people.

            <br><b> History:</b> The first jigsaw puzzle was created in the 1760s by John Spilsbury, a British mapmaker,
            as an
            educational tool. Early puzzles were made by pasting maps onto wood and cutting them into pieces. The term
            "jigsaw" comes from the tool used to cut the pieces, which resembled the teeth of a saw.

            <br> <b> Popularity: </b>Jigsaw puzzles have remained popular for centuries and are a common form of
            entertainment and a
            family activity. They are often enjoyed during leisure time, as a solo activity or with family and friends.

            <br> <b> Collectibles: </b>Some jigsaw puzzle enthusiasts collect rare and vintage puzzles, and there is a
            niche market
            for collectible puzzles with unique designs and historical significance.

            Overall, jigsaw puzzles are a timeless and engaging form of entertainment that provides both mental
            stimulation and relaxation for people of all ages.
        </div>
    </div>

